ALVA — Universal Grounded Melee Step-in and Complete Removal of Attack Steering

Objective

Implement two new, strict, universal gameplay rules across Alva:

1. Every eligible grounded melee attack must automatically perform a slight Step-in (Attack Lunge), unless that move’s actual, deliberately authored mechanics already determine that it should or should not Step-in.
2. Completely remove Attack Steering (Attack Mobility) from the game. Players and CPUs must no longer be able to move their fighters by holding Run/left/right during an ongoing attack or combat-move animation.

These rules must apply to all current and future fighters, human players, and CPU-controlled fighters.

This is a real combat-engine change, not an animation-only adjustment, character-by-character balancing patch, or documentation update.

Important: This request supersedes the repository’s previous max specification and any existing documentation requiring Attack Steering, attack-mobility tiers, or steering during attacks. Do not implement the old policy that makes ordinary attacks steerable. The new policy is the opposite: Attack Steering must be fully removed.

The two requirements must remain independent:

* Step-in is automatic forward movement authored by an eligible melee attack.
* Attack Steering is movement caused by holding or changing directional input while an attack animation plays.

Keep Step-in. Eliminate Attack Steering.

Preserve genuine, intentionally designed movement mechanics belonging to individual moves. Do not confuse automatic attack motion, existing momentum, or external physical forces with Attack Steering.

