PART 5 — COMPLETELY REMOVE ATTACK STEERING / ATTACK MOBILITY

5.1 This is a total removal, not a reduction

Attack Steering must be fully removed from Alva.

Players must no longer be able to move the fighter left or right through ordinary locomotion during an ongoing attack animation.

Holding Run, changing direction, reversing direction, or pressing directional movement must not introduce horizontal acceleration or steering while an attack controls the fighter.

This applies during:

* Startup
* Active frames
* Recovery
* Grounded melee attacks
* Aerial melee attacks
* Projectile-throwing attacks
* Extra attacks
* Deflect animations
* Technique casts
* Summon startup animations
* Ordinary moves
* Special abilities
* Moves with zero cooldown
* Moves with three-second cooldowns
* Moves with five-second cooldowns
* Any other attack or move execution state previously governed by Attack Mobility

There is no longer a category of attacks that remains steerable because it is quick, ordinary, zero-cooldown, non-Special, or airborne.

Do not preserve the previous policy where ordinary moves could steer but Specials or cooldown moves could not.

That entire Attack Steering policy is obsolete.

5.2 Remove the attack-mobility tier system

Alva currently defines:

