PART 7 — CPU INTELLIGENCE MUST FOLLOW THE SAME RULES

7.1 Player and CPU mechanical parity

All movement rules must be authoritative and shared.

A CPU executing a move must behave physically like a player executing that move from the same initial state.

This includes:

* The same automatic Step-in eligibility
* The same Step-in timing
* The same forward impulse
* The same movement restrictions
* The same collision and friction
* The same carried momentum
* The same scripted motion
* The same lack of Attack Steering

No CPU-only movement bonuses.

No CPU-only attack steering.

No special exception for Hard or Brutal difficulty.

Difficulty can change planning quality, not the mechanical rules.

